      "question": "At what time are PostgreSQL backups checked?",
      "status_code": 200,
      "wall_ms": 2496.36,
      "response": {
        "answer": "PostgreSQL backups are checked every morning at 08:00.",
        "abstained": false,
        "citations": [
          {
            "source_type": "chunk",
            "document_id": "6572506a-482b-4431-bee7-eb0c3451d6a8",
            "document_name": "operations-runbook.md",
            "chunk_id": 276,
            "chunk_index": 2,
            "content": "the secondary becomes incident commander until a lead assigns a replacement. The note should not include credentials.\n\n## Backup checks\nPostgreSQL backups are checked every morning at 08:00. The daily check confirms the latest backup completed and that its checksum matches the stored manifest. A restore drill is run once each quarter in an isolated environment. The backup operator records failures in the operations ticket queue and pages on-call if two consecutive checks fail."
          }
        ],
